# CLIENT desktop (laptop/chromebook/desktop) ONLY — copied into the sysroot by
# build-x86-host-stage4.sh solely for ROLE_CLIENT (nodes don't run X). The complete
# set of USE changes the desktop payload needs, from `emerge --pretend --autounmask`
# replayed against the build sysroot:
#   freetype[harfbuzz] — the GTK3 stack (pango → openbox/lxpanel/lightdm-gtk-greeter)
#   libdom[xml]        — www-client/netsurf (svgtiny/svg)
#   nftables[...]      — net-firewall/firewalld backend (FD-06 shields-up)
#   libdrm[radeon]     — xf86-video-ati DDX pulled by xorg-drivers (VIDEO_CARDS radeon*)
#   discover[flatpak]  — the desktop-app-governance store backend (FD-09 inc 7 /
#                        admin-bff #115): builds Discover's Flatpak backend so the
#                        provision_desktop_governance() Flatpak-remote config has a
#                        backend to drive; pulls sys-apps/flatpak. Other backends
#                        (snap/firmware/webengine) left OFF — the governed store is
#                        Flatpak-over-OCI only. (Discover's Qt6/KF6 deps are
#                        Qt6-native packages, NOT gated by the make.conf -qt6, so
#                        no qt USE override is needed here.)
media-libs/freetype harfbuzz
net-libs/libdom xml
net-firewall/nftables python json xtables
x11-libs/libdrm video_cards_radeon
kde-plasma/discover flatpak
# Discover's Qt6/appstream stack tightened in newer releases (the note above is now
# stale): the AppStream backend needs qt6, xdg-utils' man pages need xmlto[text], and
# qtmultimedia (pulled via the KF6/Qt6 multimedia libs) has REQUIRED_USE
# "vaapi? ( opengl )" — vaapi is on from the GPU profile, so opengl must be too.
# These apply to BOTH thin and thick (both ship Discover), hence desktop not capable.
dev-libs/appstream qt6
app-text/xmlto text
# Discover is a Qt6/QML Plasma app: it pulls purpose -> prison[qml] and the wider
# KF6/Qt6 QML framework stack. These modules USE-match qtbase[opengl=,vulkan=] and
# need qml, so enable opengl/vulkan/qml across the chain. qtbase also needs
# libproxy/icu/wayland for the Plasma libs. Shared by thin AND thick (both ship
# Discover); thick's capable file only ADDS the heavier app-specific flags on top.
# (Entries for modules a given weight doesn't pull are simply ignored by portage.)
dev-qt/qtbase opengl libproxy icu wayland
dev-qt/qtmultimedia qml opengl
dev-qt/qttools opengl
dev-qt/qtdeclarative opengl vulkan
dev-qt/qtquick3d opengl vulkan
dev-qt/qt5compat qml icu
kde-frameworks/prison qml
kde-frameworks/kconfig qml
kde-frameworks/sonnet qml
media-libs/mesa wayland
sys-libs/zlib minizip
x11-libs/gtk+ wayland
